Project history

PsySuite is a modular Android framework for implementing and running
psychophysical experiments on smartphones and tablets.

The original implementation of PsySuite was initiated during
research and development activities carried out within the
Unit for Visually Impaired People (U-VIP),
Fondazione Istituto Italiano di Tecnologia (IIT),
Genova, Italy (2018–2021).

The current 2.x series results from substantial architectural
redesign, refactoring, and continued development performed at:

IRCCS Azienda Ospedaliera Metropolitana
Genova, Italy (2022–2026).

Author and developer: Alberto Inuggi

